# ai-memory — ENTERPRISE-FEDERATION certified posture ENV template
# (v1.0.0, 3x7 cutline ruling §5.3, 2026-08-01,
#  docs/audit/3x7-v1-cutline-ruling-2026-08-01.md)
#
# Ruling §5.3: "Ship as a checked-in profile the daemon validates and
# refuses to boot against, with a boot banner echoing the *effective*
# posture. Prose checklists are unfalsifiable; a non-zero exit is
# falsifiable." This file is that checked-in profile for the
# ENTERPRISE-FEDERATION certification (§5.1 trust boundary: separately-
# administered peers within ONE accountable organisation — see
# federation.md's certified trust-boundary text before deploying this).
#
# Load before launching the daemon, e.g. (FULL CERTIFIED LAUNCH):
#
#   set -a; . /etc/ai-memory/enterprise-federation.env; set +a
#   ai-memory serve \
#     --tls-cert       /etc/ai-memory/server.crt \
#     --tls-key        /etc/ai-memory/server.key \
#     --mtls-allowlist /etc/ai-memory/peer-fingerprints.allow \
#     --quorum-peers   https://peer-a.example.org:9077,https://peer-b.example.org:9077
#
# The three --tls-cert / --tls-key / --mtls-allowlist flags and the
# config.toml `api_key` are NOT env-settable and NOT pinned by the profile
# below — they are the transport + application auth layers (federation.md
# "The three auth layers", Layer 1 mTLS + Layer 2 X-API-Key) that the
# certified posture requires but that this env file cannot carry. A
# paste-and-run WITHOUT them is asi-hard-clean at the crypto/attestation
# layer yet has NO transport confinement. Set them explicitly, and set the
# shared API key in config.toml (there is NO --api-key CLI flag):
#
#   # /etc/ai-memory/config.toml
#   api_key = "…"        # e.g. contents of /etc/ai-memory/api.key
#
# BEFORE first sync, enroll every peer's Ed25519 public key on THIS daemon
# (default AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_PEER_ENROLLMENT is strict → an un-enrolled
# x-peer-id is refused 401 peer_not_enrolled), per federation.md
# "Operator checklist" step 3 / enterprise-deployment.md §8.6:
#
#   ai-memory identity import --agent-id peer-a@host --pub peer-a@host.pub
#
# Verify BEFORE relying on it — never infer from the flags alone (the
# embedding-guard-gap lesson: verify the banner / doctor report, never
# infer behaviour from a flag being set):
#
#   ai-memory doctor --posture enterprise-federation
#
# This is the FEDERATION-CERTIFICATION superset of docs/deploy/asi-hard.env
# — layer this file ON TOP of (or instead of) that one; it engages the
# SAME `asi-hard` no-disable posture PLUS the federation-specific
# additions §5.3 names beyond the generic asi-hard set. Do NOT weaken
# asi-hard to deploy this file — every asi-hard pin stays engaged.

# ── The named hardened security posture (#1961) — REQUIRED. ──────────────
# See docs/deploy/asi-hard.env for the full 27-knob pinned-set explanation
# (SSOT src/security_profile.rs::KNOBS). Every asi-hard pin is a
# prerequisite of the enterprise-federation certification (§5.3: "engaged").
AI_MEMORY_SECURITY_PROFILE=asi-hard

# ── The enterprise-federation boot-refusing gate — REQUIRED. ─────────────
# Opt-in (default OFF, byte-identical legacy boot for every deployment
# that has not certified). When truthy, the daemon machine-checks the
# federation-specific additions below (peer enrollment / per-message sig
# / nonce / push-namespace-scope confinement / governance permissions
# mode / governance fail-open / trust domain / peer fingerprints / peer
# attestation JSON shape / the two must-be-UNSET federation trust
# bypasses / at-rest encryption / plaintext-peer refusal) IN ADDITION TO
# the asi-hard set above, and REFUSES TO BOOT — naming every failing
# control with its exact remediation — if ANY of them deviates.
# See src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs.
AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE=1

# ── At-rest encryption (#228) — REQUIRED. ─────────────────────────────────
# Requires a binary BUILT with `--features sqlcipher` (this env var alone
# is not sufficient — `ai-memory doctor --posture enterprise-federation`
# reports the compiled-feature state explicitly rather than letting the
# env var imply behaviour that isn't there).
AI_MEMORY_ENCRYPT_AT_REST=1

# ── Append-only audit spine (#1823 / #2954) — REQUIRED. ───────────────────
# Arms the signed `memory_revisions` ledger so every content-destroying
# mutation — INCLUDING a federation newer-wins LWW overwrite
# (`insert_if_newer` / `apply_remote_memory`, #2954) — leaves an identity-only
# SUPERSEDE leaf instead of silently replacing durable content. Certified
# posture check #19 requires this AND a provisioned daemon audit signing key
# (see the audit-custody key dirs below): an UNSIGNED leaf is tamper-evident in
# name only. Boots the same byte-identical legacy path when unset — the gate
# only refuses when AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE is armed.
AI_MEMORY_APPEND_ONLY=1

# ── Federation-specific additions §5.3 names beyond the asi-hard set. ────
# All six already default to the certified value (documented per-knob in
# CLAUDE.md's env table) — uncommented here ONLY so the effective posture
# is explicit in the boot banner (`security.posture.enterprise_federation`
# target, `daemon_runtime::run`, gated on
# AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE — see
# src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs), per the ruling's "echoing the
# *effective* posture" requirement, not because leaving them unset would
# fail the gate. #2911 added POLICY_CURRENT so an explicit `=0` cannot
# silently escape the certified set (the live FED-RQ-03 receive gate).
AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_PEER_ENROLLMENT=1
AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_SIG=1
AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_NONCE=1
AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_PUSH_NAMESPACE_SCOPE=1
AI_MEMORY_FED_REQUIRE_POLICY_CURRENT=1
AI_MEMORY_PERMISSIONS_MODE=enforce

# ── Per-deployment values — REQUIRED, operator-supplied. ─────────────────
# No sensible fleet-wide default exists for these; the boot gate REFUSES
# (naming this exact var) when any is absent. Uncomment + set:
#
# AI_MEMORY_FED_TRUST_DOMAIN=<this-fleet-identifier>
# AI_MEMORY_FED_PEER_FINGERPRINTS=/etc/ai-memory/peer-fingerprints.pins
# AI_MEMORY_FED_PEER_ATTESTATION={"peer-a":{"allowed_namespaces":["team-x/*"]},"peer-b":{"allowed_namespaces":["team-y/*"]}}
#
# `AI_MEMORY_FED_PEER_ATTESTATION` MUST be valid JSON — a malformed value
# REFUSES boot rather than silently falling back to faith-based
# replication (#2504). No peer scope's `allowed_namespaces` may contain a
# bare `**` (a deliberate per-peer allow-all) — the certified posture
# forbids it; scope every peer to its real namespace set.
#
# ── Which identity lane is this? (legacy fingerprint + attestation) ──────
# The CERTIFIED enterprise-federation posture stands up the LEGACY
# transport/identity lane: the mTLS fingerprint allowlist
# (--mtls-allowlist) + AI_MEMORY_FED_PEER_FINGERPRINTS outbound pinning +
# per-peer AI_MEMORY_FED_PEER_ATTESTATION JSON + per-peer `.pub` Ed25519
# enrollment (`ai-memory identity import`, federation.md "Operator
# checklist" step 3). It does NOT require the zero-touch CA-rooted
# credential system (AI_MEMORY_FED_TRUST_BUNDLE_DIR / _CRED_PATH /
# _CRED_CHAIN_PATH / _INVENTORY_PATH, docs/federation-identity.md).
# The zero-touch layer composes ON TOP and removes O(N^2) manual `.pub`
# exchange as a fleet grows, but it is OPTIONAL — do not set those vars
# unless you are adopting it. Stand up this lane first.

# ── Peer URLs — REQUIRED. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https:// only for every non-loopback peer. The asi-hard pin above already
# refuses AI_MEMORY_FED_ALLOW_PLAINTEXT_PEERS truthy; do NOT set it here.
# --quorum-peers / --peers must all be https:// (loopback http:// stays
# exempt on every posture — see docs/deploy/asi-hard.env).

# ── Must stay UNSET (the two federation trust bypasses). ─────────────────
# Both loosen identity/anti-replay gating and are refused by the boot gate
# if set truthy. Leave absent — do NOT uncomment.
# AI_MEMORY_FED_SYNC_TRUST_PEER=1
# AI_MEMORY_FED_TRUST_BODY_AGENT_ID=1

# ── Inference-plane egress posture (#1963, R68/D14) — recommended. ───────
# See docs/deploy/asi-hard.env for the full explanation.
AI_MEMORY_INFERENCE_EGRESS=loopback-only

# ── Audit-custody key enrollment — REQUIRED for a clean verify-audit-trail
#    under asi-hard. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The asi-hard profile (SSOT src/security_profile.rs::KNOBS) PINS four
# require-modes ON:
#   AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_WITNESS          — dual-chain audit-head witness anchor
#   AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ROLE_SEPARATION  — three-key Recorder/Judge/Stopper sep.
#   AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_IDENTITY_LINEAGE — identity-lineage succession chain
#   AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ROLLBACK_CHECK   — open-time rollback-evidence head check
# Those pins only BECOME cryptographically load-bearing once the matching
# custody KEY material is enrolled. A require-mode with NO enrolled key is
# DIRTY (exit 1), not withheld — so under asi-hard these are REQUIRED, not
# merely recommended, to get a clean `ai-memory verify-audit-trail`.
# Point each dir at a mount the daemon can READ but a compromised daemon
# process cannot OVERWRITE:
#
#   AI_MEMORY_WITNESS_KEY_DIR=/etc/ai-memory/witness-keys       # signer (audit-witness.priv)
#   AI_MEMORY_WITNESS_PUBKEY=<base64-url-nopad-32-bytes>        # K1 pin (verify-side)
#   AI_MEMORY_RECORDER_KEY_DIR=/etc/ai-memory/recorder-keys     # role: Recorder signer
#   AI_MEMORY_RECORDER_PUBKEY=<base64-url-nopad-32-bytes>       # Recorder pin
#   AI_MEMORY_JUDGE_KEY_DIR=/etc/ai-memory/judge-keys           # role: Judge signer
#   AI_MEMORY_JUDGE_PUBKEY=<base64-url-nopad-32-bytes>          # Judge pin
#   AI_MEMORY_STOPPER_KEY_DIR=/etc/ai-memory/stopper-keys       # role: Stopper signer
#   AI_MEMORY_STOPPER_PUBKEY=<base64-url-nopad-32-bytes>        # Stopper pin
#   AI_MEMORY_OPERATOR_PUBKEY=<base64-32-bytes>                 # governance operator key
#                                                               # (ALSO enrolls as an R40 approver —
#                                                               #  satisfies posture check #20, #2991)
#   AI_MEMORY_APPROVER_PUBKEYS=<b64>,<b64>                      # extra R40 m-of-n approver keys (optional)
# (The enrolled recorder/judge/stopper pubkeys MUST be pairwise-distinct.)
# Identity lineage additionally needs an enrolled genesis succession record
# (`agent_lineage`); rollback-check needs the off-table head-anchor.log on
# the witness mount.
#
# ── doctor --posture is NOT verify-audit-trail — an HONEST distinction. ───
# `ai-memory doctor --posture enterprise-federation` machine-checks the
# 20 BOOT-time federation controls (enrollment / sig / nonce / scope /
# fingerprints / attestation JSON / at-rest / plaintext-peer refusal /
# append-only-audit-spine-armed #2954 / R40-escalate-producer-armable #2991
# — the last requires an enrolled approver key, above, so the wired L1-6
# escalate producer routes to a SATISFIABLE signed-approval gate; etc.
# — src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs). It does NOT check the four
# audit-custody require-modes above; those are consumed by a SEPARATE
# command, `ai-memory verify-audit-trail` (src/governance/audit.rs, both
# backends). CONSEQUENCE: a node can BOOT clean and PASS
# `doctor --posture enterprise-federation` while `verify-audit-trail`
# reports DIRTY — precisely because the pinned require-modes have no
# enrolled key yet. Run BOTH as part of the certified stand-up; do not
# read a green `doctor --posture` as proof the audit spine is anchored.
